@startuml
!theme plain
title Acquiring Timeout / Reversal Decision — Synthetic Reference
participant Merchant
participant "Payment Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Orchestrator" as Orch
participant "Acquirer Adapter" as Adapter
participant "Acquiring Switch" as Switch
participant "Recovery Worker" as Worker
Merchant -> Gateway : authorize with idempotency key
Gateway -> Orch : submit attempt
Orch -> Adapter : authorization request
Adapter -> Switch : network submission
... Response lost after dispatch ...
Adapter --> Orch : transport timeout
Orch -> Orch : persist UNKNOWN; retain references
Orch --> Gateway : unknown / pending outcome
Gateway --> Merchant : pending; do not retry charge blindly
Orch -> Worker : enqueue authoritative inquiry
Worker -> Adapter : query by supported references
Adapter -> Switch : status lookup / reconciliation
alt Authorization confirmed
 Switch --> Adapter : approved
 Adapter --> Worker : approved
 Worker -> Orch : transition to AUTHORIZED
 opt Merchant wants to cancel and rules permit
 Orch -> Adapter : request contract-supported reversal
 Adapter -> Switch : reversal / void with required references
 Switch --> Adapter : reversal status
 Adapter --> Orch : record reversal lifecycle
 end
else Decline confirmed
 Switch --> Adapter : declined
 Adapter --> Worker : declined
 Worker -> Orch : transition to DECLINED
else Still unknown
 Switch --> Adapter : not resolved
 Adapter --> Worker : pending
 Worker -> Worker : backoff and escalate by deadline
end
note over Worker,Switch
Do not assume a reversal is automatically
required or permitted for every timeout.
end note
@enduml